    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Tuscarawas River once carried travelers south, while Turkeyfoot Lake—named for a noted Indian chief—was the county’s largest body of water and a haven for hunters.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
