      ],
      "source": "https://www.newfranklin.org/1179/History"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "A well‑traveled line of the Underground Railroad crossed the township before 1860, helping runaway slaves reach Canada.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.newfranklin.org/1179/History"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "In 1997 residents incorporated the village of New Franklin to prevent annexation by neighboring cities.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/New_Franklin%2C_Ohio"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "New Franklin officially became a city on March 5 2006 after a municipal merger that took effect January 1 2005.",
